# BUGS

`strerror` truncates a message longer than 39 bytes: `EDOM` gives `Mathematics argument out of domain of f`, and `EOVERFLOW` gives `Value too large to be stored in data ty`.
`strerror_r` with a large enough buffer does not.

The functions do not test their arguments: a null pointer faults.

`<string.h>` declares no `strstr`, `strtok`, `strcpy`, `strncat`, `strpbrk`, `strspn`, `strcspn`, `strcoll`, `strxfrm` or `memccpy`.
